WEBVTT

00:00:07.484 --> 00:00:13.904
Candy was surprised when she found out
that Annie keeps sending letters to Archie every week.

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:25.220
When Annie left, with whom she lived since
her earliest days, Candy felt very lonely.

00:00:32.943 --> 00:00:39.335
A wonderful Sunday.

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.167
I see, yes, I think that as well!

00:00:49.621 --> 00:00:53.480
Say, Patty, everybody seems to be having
a good time, what's going on?

00:00:54.296 --> 00:00:56.566
Fifth Sunday is drawing near.

00:00:57.633 --> 00:01:00.738
You mean, Fifth Sunday?
(The same thing, but said in Japanese)

00:01:01.563 --> 00:01:04.942
It's a time when students are allowed
to leave the school premises.

00:01:04.977 --> 00:01:07.454
-So they'll let us outside?
-Yes.

00:01:07.664 --> 00:01:09.727
Wow, I'll stretch my wings!

00:01:12.524 --> 00:01:14.705
I didn't mean that literally...

00:01:15.359 --> 00:01:17.519
Have I said something wrong?

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:27.509
Fifth Sunday? So they're doing this
only a few times a year.

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:31.320
As expected from St. Paul academy,
they're so shrewd.

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:36.918
Kurin!

00:01:41.211 --> 00:01:46.362
Good news, Kurin! I'll be allowed to go out
for a whole day on the next Sunday!

00:01:49.875 --> 00:01:53.039
I guess I'll go sightseeing with Stear and Archie.

00:01:54.155 --> 00:02:00.747
Tower bridge... St. Paul's cathedral...
That's right! We might ride a boat on Thames!

00:02:04.698 --> 00:02:09.115
Thus, the eagerly awaited Fifth Sunday finally arrived.

00:02:14.172 --> 00:02:16.861
-Mother!
-Father!

00:02:19.775 --> 00:02:22.221
The air outside feels so good!

00:02:22.222 --> 00:02:24.667
Mr. Alistear! Mr. Archibald!

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:28.977
-Brother, it's that carriage!
-So nice from them to send a carriage for us.

00:02:29.398 --> 00:02:31.551
This way!

00:02:31.741 --> 00:02:35.449
I'm sorry, but could you wait a little?
We're waiting for Candy.

00:02:35.835 --> 00:02:38.169
Everyone is already waiting for you.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.081
That's our Candy, she's a fast one!

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:44.625
Please.

00:02:51.654 --> 00:02:53.348
-Neil?
-Eliza!

00:02:53.522 --> 00:02:57.374
You look surprised. Grand aunt Elroy
is waiting in the hotel.

00:02:57.887 --> 00:02:59.292
Where is Candy?

00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.607
-Hurry! Go!
-As you wish.

00:03:03.356 --> 00:03:05.260
Hey, but Candy isn't...

00:03:15.142 --> 00:03:17.170
Took me some time to dress up!

00:03:19.011 --> 00:03:20.508
Teacher, I'm off!

00:03:20.816 --> 00:03:22.834
Where are you going, Candice?

00:03:23.582 --> 00:03:26.809
What do you mean, "where am I going"...
...you must be kidding me!

00:03:27.402 --> 00:03:31.759
Even though I'm a freshman,
I know about a Fifth Sunday...

00:03:31.794 --> 00:03:35.362
Candice, regulations don't allow us
to let you leave.

00:03:35.363 --> 00:03:36.843
Regulations...?

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:43.132
Even though today is the Fifth Sunday, unless your parents
or relatives give us permission to let you go,

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:45.077
...we can't let you leave the premises.

00:03:45.112 --> 00:03:46.791
But...

00:03:49.506 --> 00:03:52.767
Now, return to your room.
Prepare for tomorrow's lecture.

00:03:55.506 --> 00:03:56.715
Teacher...!

00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:16.230
I thought this was going all too well...

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:23.144
Kurin, no good.

00:04:30.895 --> 00:04:32.073
The yard...

00:04:32.796 --> 00:04:35.503
That's right! In that case,
I'll go to the other Pony's hill!

00:04:35.538 --> 00:04:36.939
I'll feel better over there.

00:04:43.781 --> 00:04:45.032
Wait up, Kurin!

00:04:54.128 --> 00:04:59.697
If this were the real Pony's hill,
and if I were together with Annie,

00:05:00.931 --> 00:05:02.798
...just how happy would we be?

00:05:18.012 --> 00:05:19.306
What's the matter, Kurin?

00:05:22.931 --> 00:05:25.218
Fire! Hurry, water...!

00:05:25.594 --> 00:05:26.394
Water!

00:05:28.578 --> 00:05:29.869
You are...

00:05:32.883 --> 00:05:35.273
What's up with all the panic?

00:05:39.496 --> 00:05:41.611
Terrius... you...

00:05:42.401 --> 00:05:45.045
...you're smoking here...

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.417
You look envious, miss Stutter.

00:05:47.629 --> 00:05:49.543
If you want some, I'll let you have one.

00:05:50.176 --> 00:05:51.739
You must be kidding me!

00:05:52.422 --> 00:05:56.322
Don't make that face!
Your freckles really stand out that way!

00:05:59.919 --> 00:06:03.373
You know, when your nose moves,
your freckles move as well.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:08.407
Hey, I don't want you to speak that way
about my freckles!

00:06:08.595 --> 00:06:10.102
Why do you break the rules, anyway?

00:06:10.137 --> 00:06:15.184
Oh, since you don't like being called after
your freckles, maybe you're a Tarzan-girl.

00:06:15.882 --> 00:06:17.871
What's a Tarzan-girl?

00:06:18.245 --> 00:06:22.983
In the darkness, throwing a white rope,
and swiftly, escaping like an animal...

00:06:26.322 --> 00:06:32.204
And, holding onto the end of the rope,
dashing from girls' ward over to boys' ward!

00:06:39.862 --> 00:06:41.582
He was watching me.

00:06:41.958 --> 00:06:44.608
When I was going to Archie's room...

00:06:45.498 --> 00:06:47.822
Hmmmh, Lady Freckles or Tarzan-girl...

00:06:47.907 --> 00:06:49.737
Both of them fit you well.

00:06:51.726 --> 00:06:54.973
How about freckled Tarzan?

00:06:55.187 --> 00:06:56.548
What's that?

00:06:57.659 --> 00:06:58.988
It's your name.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.400
My name is Candice White Adley!

00:07:02.626 --> 00:07:04.951
Don't forget that name!

00:07:05.309 --> 00:07:08.686
Alright? It's Candice White Adley!

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:13.370
Okay, okay. Heard you the first time.
Freckled Tarzan.

00:07:15.006 --> 00:07:18.224
Hey, hey, your freckles stand out
when you're angry.

00:07:18.431 --> 00:07:22.425
By the way, why are you here?
It's Fifth Sunday.

00:07:22.757 --> 00:07:24.332
And why are you here?

00:07:24.657 --> 00:07:28.313
When everybody leaves,
the school becomes so peaceful.

00:07:28.799 --> 00:07:29.994
You weirdo.

00:07:30.368 --> 00:07:34.969
That's right, this place is the other
Pony's hill, my special place!

00:07:35.252 --> 00:07:37.971
Don't just barge in and smoke in here!

00:07:42.783 --> 00:07:44.707
Other Pony's hill?

00:08:03.533 --> 00:08:05.474
You look well, everyone.

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:10.112
-Welcome to London, grand Aunt.
-Did you have a pleasant journey?

00:08:10.517 --> 00:08:11.975
It was pleasant.

00:08:12.919 --> 00:08:17.018
I brought you these presents from America.
Neil, Eliza.

00:08:17.053 --> 00:08:18.133
Thank you!

00:08:20.048 --> 00:08:21.815
I'm glad, Grand Aunt.

00:08:22.404 --> 00:08:24.735
These are for Stear and Archie.

00:08:26.723 --> 00:08:29.524
Why are you two looking at me like that?

00:08:29.611 --> 00:08:34.755
Aunt Elroy, just why did you separate Candy
from the rest of us?

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:38.497
Candy is also a member of the Adley family.

00:08:38.687 --> 00:08:40.613
Only by name.

00:08:40.841 --> 00:08:42.820
Eliza, you keep quiet.

00:08:42.821 --> 00:08:44.799
We are speaking with Aunt!

00:08:45.013 --> 00:08:48.826
I decide whether I will invite Candy or not.

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.514
Therefore, why didn't you invite her?

00:08:52.105 --> 00:08:57.913
Archie, I didn't come all the way to England
just to have something ruin my mood.

00:08:58.914 --> 00:08:59.976
Come in!

00:09:00.663 --> 00:09:01.827
A guest.

00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:03.934
Let her enter.

00:09:04.605 --> 00:09:06.315
Maybe it's Candy.

00:09:06.965 --> 00:09:07.941
Please.

00:09:15.846 --> 00:09:17.125
Annie?

00:09:17.429 --> 00:09:19.330
My, Annie Brighton.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.871
It's been a long time.

00:09:23.069 --> 00:09:26.623
-Now, join us.
-Excuse the intrusion.

00:09:37.438 --> 00:09:43.659
It seems though I and that Terrius guy
are the only ones left in this big school.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:46.901
I guess everybody is having so much fun right now.

00:09:50.167 --> 00:09:52.700
Maybe there are more students who stayed
in the school?

00:09:52.926 --> 00:09:54.121
Maybe...

00:09:56.713 --> 00:09:58.393
Nobody is in here!

00:09:58.529 --> 00:10:00.088
Candice, open up!

00:10:01.718 --> 00:10:02.895
Teacher!

00:10:02.896 --> 00:10:04.570
Hurry up, Candice!

00:10:08.508 --> 00:10:12.151
You are free to go out, hurry and prepare yourself.
A carriage is here to pick you up.

00:10:12.358 --> 00:10:15.598
To pick me up?
It means that I can go?

00:10:15.984 --> 00:10:19.202
Now, hurry. It's impolite to keep someone waiting.

00:10:19.401 --> 00:10:21.135
Yes! I'll go right now!

00:10:22.098 --> 00:10:24.996
But... I wonder just who came to pick me up.

00:10:25.031 --> 00:10:28.301
-From America...
-Stop!

00:10:28.336 --> 00:10:31.464
Teacher, let me look forward to this until
I leave the premises!

00:10:31.469 --> 00:10:32.751
Candice!

00:10:32.868 --> 00:10:35.334
You'd spoil the surprise if you told me now!

00:10:35.756 --> 00:10:38.564
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
Factual error: Tarzan first appeared in a 1914 novel.
This Candy Candy episode takes place in 1913! Oops!

00:10:45.944 --> 00:10:49.606
I wonder who came from America to pick me up...

00:10:50.358 --> 00:10:54.912
Sister Pony, sister Lane, Tom... or maybe...

00:10:56.391 --> 00:10:59.374
-Candice, hurry up!
-Okay!

00:11:00.086 --> 00:11:02.755
I'm really going this time, Kurin.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:06.447
What's the matter?

00:11:12.931 --> 00:11:14.570
Hello, Candy!

00:11:14.653 --> 00:11:16.002
Mr. Brighton!

00:11:16.872 --> 00:11:22.887
Mr. Brighton is a man who took Annie
from Pony's home, becoming her father.

00:11:23.323 --> 00:11:24.901
Now, come on.

00:11:24.936 --> 00:11:27.466
Annie... Annie is here as well?

00:11:27.881 --> 00:11:29.583
Well then, take care.

00:11:34.753 --> 00:11:35.708
Annie!

00:11:42.063 --> 00:11:43.877
Annie is in the hotel.

00:11:43.985 --> 00:11:46.243
She is waiting for me in the hotel?

00:11:46.855 --> 00:11:50.317
Meeting Annie in London...
It's a dream come true!

00:11:51.203 --> 00:11:52.630
Candy...

00:11:59.451 --> 00:12:01.034
That's the London Bridge.

00:12:01.069 --> 00:12:03.403
Annie and I used to sing about it
ever since we were little.

00:12:03.438 --> 00:12:06.558
"London bridge is falling down, falling down..."

00:12:12.884 --> 00:12:15.722
That is the Tower Bridge, right?

00:12:16.244 --> 00:12:18.691
It's rising!

00:12:20.377 --> 00:12:24.382
Take a good look! I bet you've never seen
a bridge like that one, Kurin!

00:12:25.951 --> 00:12:28.158
Candy, where do you want to go?

00:12:28.642 --> 00:12:30.875
Of course, to the hotel where Annie is!

00:12:31.693 --> 00:12:34.936
The Adleys are in the hotel, too.

00:12:35.096 --> 00:12:37.445
Then, grand aunt Elroy...

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:42.800
So that's the reason I wasn't invited.

00:12:43.329 --> 00:12:49.707
It's fine with me, but my wife doesn't want anyone to know
that both you and Annie were raised in Pony's home.

00:12:50.935 --> 00:12:53.822
I'll give up on seeing Annie then.

00:12:54.617 --> 00:12:59.314
Thank you. To make up for this, today I'll take
you anywhere you like.

00:13:00.150 --> 00:13:02.010
I want to visit some wide and open place!

00:13:02.421 --> 00:13:03.860
Such a place?

00:13:08.553 --> 00:13:10.945
I want to scream out loud!

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:12.162
Very well.

00:13:12.163 --> 00:13:14.858
-To Epsom!
-Yes!

00:13:28.516 --> 00:13:29.768
Horse racing...

00:13:29.803 --> 00:13:32.847
This is a wide, open place
where you can yell all you'd like...

00:13:33.035 --> 00:13:35.378
Moreover, there is a racing horse
which came all the way from America.

00:13:35.545 --> 00:13:37.338
A horse from America?

00:13:37.373 --> 00:13:41.703
Yes... it'll compete in the next race,
its name is "Pony flash"...

00:13:41.861 --> 00:13:43.394
Pony flash?

00:13:43.931 --> 00:13:46.471
"...from Steve's farm in America..."

00:13:47.668 --> 00:13:49.143
It's Tom's horse!

00:13:49.178 --> 00:13:50.488
You know him?

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:54.547
Yes, he was in Pony's home with me.

00:13:54.746 --> 00:13:56.752
Oh, that's nice.

00:13:57.185 --> 00:14:01.720
Mr. Brighton, so where is that horse?

00:14:07.815 --> 00:14:09.794
That must be it, mr. Brighton!

00:14:14.558 --> 00:14:17.358
Tom must have worked hard about this horse...

00:14:25.194 --> 00:14:27.607
Go, Pony flash!

00:14:32.238 --> 00:14:33.402
Terrius?

00:14:34.383 --> 00:14:41.325
You've mixed up some names. This horse is called
"Royal king", and it's going to win the next race.

00:14:42.133 --> 00:14:43.792
Mr. Brighton...

00:14:45.303 --> 00:14:47.331
Pony flash is over there.

00:14:50.558 --> 00:14:52.467
So that's Pony flash...

00:14:55.432 --> 00:14:58.929
It looks exactly like you.
It's got freckles all over!

00:14:59.255 --> 00:15:04.484
What? Does that matter, as long
as it's faster than the others?

00:15:04.906 --> 00:15:06.872
Alright. Wanna bet?

00:15:07.274 --> 00:15:08.201
Bet?

00:15:08.425 --> 00:15:13.991
If that clumsy horse takes a third or better place,
I won't call you by your freckles anymore.

00:15:14.163 --> 00:15:17.980
I'll call you Candice White Adley.

00:15:17.981 --> 00:15:18.795
Well then?

00:15:19.401 --> 00:15:20.474
Really?

00:15:21.304 --> 00:15:25.873
However, if that horse takes a fourth place,
or worse, you'll become my slave.

00:15:25.987 --> 00:15:27.032
A slave?

00:15:27.832 --> 00:15:28.921
That's right.

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.935
If I want to smoke, you'll light my cigarette.

00:15:31.970 --> 00:15:34.814
If I get thirsty, you'll make me some tea.

00:15:35.094 --> 00:15:37.081
Who'd do that...!

00:15:38.683 --> 00:15:43.564
That's right... I wonder if that
horse can finish the race at all.

00:15:44.077 --> 00:15:45.408
I'll bet you!

00:15:45.569 --> 00:15:46.894
That's the spirit!

00:15:46.895 --> 00:15:47.669
Well then!

00:15:49.261 --> 00:15:51.783
You didn't introduce him to me, Candy?

00:15:52.068 --> 00:15:54.241
He isn't a person worthy of an introduction!

00:15:59.874 --> 00:16:01.412
They've started.

00:16:03.857 --> 00:16:05.584
Pony flash!

00:16:08.512 --> 00:16:11.283
It seems that Pony flash
has trouble keeping up.

00:16:19.739 --> 00:16:22.409
Go, Pony flash!

00:16:25.145 --> 00:16:26.331
Poor thing.

00:16:30.609 --> 00:16:36.922
Pony! Tom in America is rooting for you!
Ow! Pony flash!

00:16:37.253 --> 00:16:40.189
It's catching up! Go, pony!

00:16:43.206 --> 00:16:45.368
But it's still last...

00:16:55.908 --> 00:17:00.959
Pony! Tom's friend is rooting for you!
Pony!

00:17:03.421 --> 00:17:06.470
Go, Pony! Go!!

00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.620
No good.

00:17:30.984 --> 00:17:34.593
I lose. Can I start by polishing your shoes?

00:17:35.431 --> 00:17:38.135
Looking from my seat,
your horse came in third.

00:17:38.467 --> 00:17:39.621
But...

00:17:39.718 --> 00:17:42.098
Well, time to part our ways.

00:17:44.735 --> 00:17:45.984
Terry...

00:17:47.303 --> 00:17:50.841
That's too bad. Another five meters
and our horse would've finished third.

00:17:50.876 --> 00:17:53.362
Thank you, Mr. Brighton!

00:17:55.071 --> 00:17:58.521
I haven't screamed my lungs out
for such a long time!

00:17:59.579 --> 00:18:01.220
Me, too!

00:18:01.445 --> 00:18:08.626
When I scream my lungs out, all those unpleasant and sad
things I kept inside seem to fly away from me!

00:18:09.392 --> 00:18:10.814
Candy.

00:18:11.064 --> 00:18:13.237
And it's all thanks to you, mr. Brighton!

00:18:20.425 --> 00:18:24.463
So pretty! St. Paul's cathedral is all in red!

00:18:24.714 --> 00:18:26.995
Candy, your face also looks red.

00:18:27.682 --> 00:18:31.145
Mr. Brighton, you too... and Kurin, as well!

00:18:49.054 --> 00:18:56.583
Candy, from time to time,
I start thinking how we, Brightons,

00:18:56.618 --> 00:18:59.925
...would have changed
if we adopted you instead of Annie.

00:19:00.151 --> 00:19:01.637
Mr. Brighton?

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:11.560
No... Annie is a good girl. So calm, pure...

00:19:12.193 --> 00:19:15.220
That's right! Unlike me, she is so much more...

00:19:15.611 --> 00:19:21.565
Actually, the reason I met up with you today
is because I want you to take care of Annie.

00:19:22.010 --> 00:19:23.531
Annie?

00:19:24.154 --> 00:19:27.455
Annie is going to transfer to your school.

00:19:28.557 --> 00:19:30.585
To St. Paul academy?

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:35.796
Thus, my wife and Annie went to
Adleys' place to greet them.

00:19:37.139 --> 00:19:39.629
However, I came to see you.

00:19:39.874 --> 00:19:40.741
Me?

00:19:40.878 --> 00:19:47.742
The one who cares and worries the most about Annie,
the one I can rely on, is you, Candy.

00:19:47.833 --> 00:19:51.187
But if someone finds out
about Annie and I, Annie will...

00:19:52.046 --> 00:19:55.304
That's the problem.
It's a selfish favor to ask,

00:19:55.339 --> 00:19:59.725
...I'd like you to take care of Annie,
because that's something you always did.

00:20:07.298 --> 00:20:08.740
You don't want that, Candy?

00:20:09.409 --> 00:20:12.820
No, it's just... I'm a little jealous of Annie.

00:20:12.934 --> 00:20:14.002
How come?

00:20:14.842 --> 00:20:17.482
It's because she has such a kind father.

00:20:18.347 --> 00:20:21.615
Mr. Brighton, I'll do all I can.

00:20:22.443 --> 00:20:24.298
Thank you, Candy.

00:20:28.695 --> 00:20:31.884
Kurin, Annie is coming to St. Paul academy.

00:20:32.109 --> 00:20:33.305
Though not immediately,
I'm sure that one day...

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:36.477
...we'll be good friends,
just like we were back in Pony's home.

00:20:56.461 --> 00:21:02.329
Seeing mr. Brighton's strong posture,
Candy remembered the big tree back at Pony's home,

00:21:02.364 --> 00:21:13.792
...the tree that ever so gently watched over Annie,
making Candy feel very envious.

00:21:15.141 --> 00:21:20.246
To be continued...
